e print and the profound  implications of this decision  we are confident that a close  examination of the implications of nato  enlargement will lead this country away  from this mistaken policy  let me just add a little bit from the  right  on john's challenge to the state  department to debate us the coalition  against nato expansion in cities all  over america  the state department loves to go around  the world preaching the merits of  democracy to all and sundry well we're  challenging them to practice it  and if they refuse to discuss this vital  commitment  before the american people in debates  around this country in the major cities  where ordinary people can come and  listen  then let us hear no more can't from them  about the merits of democracy because  they don't mean a word of it  we do intend to take  our campaign against nato enlargement to  the american people  we realize that the answer to the money  being promised on capitol hill through  the defense contractors is the voices of  ordinary american citizens  we are fortunate to have in our initial  coalition  two organizations which have a great  deal of strength at the grassroots  and we're going to ask them to come  forward now and say a little bit about  what they're going to do  to take the question of nato enlargement  to the american people i would like to  call first on chris artizone from eagle  forum  thank you very much my name is chris  artizone and i'm the executive director  of eagle forum and it is with pleasure  that we join in this coalition um  against the expansion of nato this is an  unusual coalition it has members of from  all across the political spectrum um and  this really reflects the ideas and  thoughts of the american people  one of the great things about our system  of government is that when the people  speak out our elected representatives do  listen and at eagle forum we are  committed to taking this message to  grassroots americans  and have them speak out about their  thoughts about it  with the expansion of nato comes many  questions that haven't been answered  and probably many of them are not even  answerable who will be  who  will we be protecting the nato countries  from why admit some of the warsaw pac  countries and not others and how much is  it going to cost us both in dollars and  u.s lives  the biggest question is why should  americans commit to defend far away  european borders that have been the  locus of ethics ethnic nationalist and  religious disputes for hundreds of years  make no mistake about it nato is a life  and death u.s promise to go to war to  protect the other members  the american people deserve the  opportunity to be heard and at eagle  forum we are going to take the message  to our grassroots and to grassroots  americans of all various uh political  stripes and get them to speak out about  what they believe  a sound foreign policy and national  defense strategy for our country is and  some people ask  eagle forum is a conservative grassroots  quote unquote pro-family organization  why would you all be interested in this  issue  we have long been interested in sound  foreign affairs and a strong national  defense policy because without strong  national defense and sound foreign  affairs you can't have strong families  and our members are very interested in  this issue and a variety of other issues  that have to do with foreign affairs and  they are very excited to get involved to  talk to their senators i mean even the  members of the house we are calling on  the house to hold hearings on the budget  issues and to hold real debates on what  this will mean to the future of our  armed forces  and the future of our country and so we  encourage both houses of congress to  hold extensive hearings and to listen to  what the american people are saying on  this vital issue thank you  and from the left gordon clark of peace  action  hi my name is gordon clark i'm the  executive director of peace action  form