y initiative truly  the greatest one to go on since the  beginning of the cold war over 50 years  ago we think the american people should  be worried when official washington gets  together and says as john has said it's  a done deal nothing to worry about  we think the american people should be  worried when official washington gets  together and says that there's going to  be virtually no cost attached to  defending a new continent in a major  policy initiative we certainly think  that the american people should be  worried and should be clutching their  wallets and pocket books when officials  from lockheed martin the world's largest  military contractor is leading the  lobbying effort to push this new foreign  policy initiative of nato expansion  perhaps worst of all for us and i think  worst for american democracy again is  the complete lack of public and media  debate on this issue so far there used  to be a time in this country when public  debate on major foreign policy issues  was considered the norm and not the  exception and quite frankly at this  point i feel that there has been less  public and media debate on this issue  than there has been pregame analysis of  the most recent super bowl and i would  also add a look at what official  estimates of that game turned out to be  because official washington and clinton  the congress the state department  doesn't seem to have any real interest  in sponsoring true debate in the  american public on this historic  initiative it's up to us uh  organizations grassroots organizations  to do that and that is exactly what we  intend to do  this coming wednesday  will be the launching of the nate no to  nato expansion debate uh which is going  to be happening at 15 cities across  america from new york washington dc  atlanta los angeles san francisco  seattle and a number of cities in  between  people who are joining us on this tour  include dr alla yaroshinskaya whose  advisor to president yeltsin and a  former member